'''Carlton Lee Haselrig''' (January 22, 1966 – July 22, 2020) was an American [[Wrestling weight classes|heavyweight wrestler]] and [[National Football League]] (NFL) player. Haselrig wrestled for [[University of Pittsburgh at Johnstown]]. He is the only person to ever win six [[National Collegiate Athletic Association|NCAA]] titles in [[Collegiate wrestling|wrestling]], three times in [[NCAA Division II|Division II]] and three times in [[NCAA Division I|Division I]]. His three-peat of [[NCAA Division II Wrestling Championships|Division II]] and [[NCAA Division I Wrestling Championships|Division I NCAA National Championships]] were won in 1987, 1988, and 1989. All six championships were won for [[University of Pittsburgh at Johnstown|Pitt–Johnstown]].<ref>{{Cite web|title=Carlton Haselrig |url=http://www.wrestlinghalloffame.org/wrestlers.php?wrestler=1399 |work=wrestlinghalloffame.org |publisher=[[National Wrestling Hall of Fame and Museum]] |accessdate=March 23, 2010 }}{{dead link|date=November 2016 |bot=InternetArchiveBot |fix-attempted=yes }}</ref>

Haselrig then moved on to professional [[American football|football]], where he played five seasons in the NFL, becoming a [[Pro Bowl]] offensive guard in 1993. In 2008, he made his [[mixed martial arts]] debut in [[Atlantic City, New Jersey]]. In 2016, Haselrig was inducted into the [[National Wrestling Hall of Fame and Museum|National Wrestling Hall of Fame]] as a Distinguished Member.

